# ROUND in each round state on values at the ends of the 32-bit range:
# 2^31 - 1, minus 20 and 63, and -2^31, plus 1, 20 and 63. Glyph g sets
# state g (RTG, RTHG, RTDG, RDTG, RUTG, SROUND 0x48, 0xB0 and 0xF8, S45ROUND
# 0xB0, 0xB8, 0x40 and 0x78, SROUND 0xC8, S45ROUND 0xF8, ROFF); for value i, point 2i gets the result and
# point 2i + 1 the result minus the value, each clamped to 2^22.
# Observed: the arithmetic wraps in 32 bits; a result whose sign differs from
# the value's becomes 0, or 32 for RTHG and the phase for SROUND and S45ROUND,
# with the value's sign; SROUND takes values down to a multiple of its
# period, S45ROUND towards zero; the reserved period (3) is one grid period.
heights 16384
wraps-at-32-bits
fpgm
  PUSH 0; FDEF; ENDF
end
